  "title": "OpenTelemetry log record fixtures (authored)",
  "description": "Two authored benign bases (a 32-character lowercase hex trace id built by hand, and the upper-case trace id example printed in the OTLP specification) and nine hand-written OTLP/JSON log records that project them: the two existing authored GitHub classic personal access token bases (a and b, reused, not re-authored) placed in a body string, a nested map and array body, an attribute, exception text, a resource attribute and a body string holding serialized JSON, plus one record with both tokens, and two identifier-only records. Every record carries a trace id and a span id. Synthetic: the tokens are the existing fake word runs padded with zeros, never issued, and the record structure is an evidence-derived construction from the OpenTelemetry data model and OTLP/JSON encoding, not an observed log. None was tested against any service. The independent base count is four (two token bases, two identifier bases); the nine projections are correlated.",
